  "PROFESSIONAL / ACTIVE": "PROFESSIONEEL / ACTIEF",
  "Progressed from Software Engineering Intern to IFSF Technical Support and then Full-time Embedded Software Engineer.": "Doorgegroeid van Software Engineering Intern naar IFSF Technical Support en daarna fulltime Embedded Software Engineer.",
  "IFSF PUBLICATIONS": "IFSF-PUBLICATIES",
  "Sep 2024 — Present": "sep 2024 — heden",
  "Professional · Team environment · Active": "Professioneel · teamomgeving · actief",
  "Work across hardware, network, protocol, and API boundaries": "Werk over de grenzen van hardware, netwerk, protocol en API heen",
  "Develop embedded and systems-level software primarily in C++, communicate with industrial devices and operational-technology networks, bridge established communication protocols with modern software architectures, and develop REST/HTTP functionality.": "Ontwikkelt embedded en systems-level software voornamelijk in C++, communiceert met industriële apparaten en OT-netwerken, verbindt bestaande communicatieprotocollen met moderne softwarearchitecturen en ontwikkelt REST/HTTP-functionaliteit.",
  "02 / CAREER PROGRESSION": "02 / LOOPBAANONTWIKKELING",
  "Software Engineering Intern → IFSF Technical Support → Embedded Software Engineer": "Software Engineering Intern → IFSF Technical Support → Embedded Software Engineer",
  "The progression combines implementation, technical support, industrial protocol investigation, interoperability research, and formal engineering documentation.": "De ontwikkeling combineert implementatie, technische ondersteuning, onderzoek naar industriële protocollen, interoperabiliteitsonderzoek en formele engineeringdocumentatie.",
  "03 / EVIDENCE": "03 / BEWIJS",
  "Connected professional work": "Verbonden professioneel werk",
  "ILAC and IFSF Engineering Bulletins 26 and 27 sit under Haia because they are professional work, not personal projects.": "ILAC en IFSF Engineering Bulletins 26 en 27 vallen onder Haia omdat het professioneel werk is en geen persoonlijke projecten zijn.",
  "PROFESSIONAL CASE STUDY / POC": "PROFESSIONELE CASESTUDY / POC",
  "A compatibility bridge between the OpenRetailing Price Pole API Collections and installed IFSF LON Price Pole equipment.": "Een compatibiliteitsbrug tussen de OpenRetailing Price Pole API Collections en geïnstalleerde IFSF LON Price Pole-apparatuur.",
  "PUBLICATIONS": "PUBLICATIES",
  "HAIA WORK": "HAIA-WERK",
  "Embedded Software Engineer · Individual contributor": "Embedded Software Engineer · individuele bijdrager",
  "Proof of concept demonstrated to IFSF Working Group": "Proof of concept gedemonstreerd aan de IFSF Working Group",
  "Modern API clients, installed legacy OT": "Moderne API-cliënten, geïnstalleerde legacy-OT",
  "Forecourt environments can contain installed Price Pole equipment built around IFSF LON while newer systems expose REST-based OpenRetailing Price Pole APIs. The engineering problem is translating between endpoint-oriented API resources and the IFSF database/message model without forcing immediate field replacement.": "Forecourt-omgevingen kunnen geïnstalleerde Price Pole-apparatuur op basis van IFSF LON bevatten, terwijl nieuwere systemen REST-gebaseerde OpenRetailing Price Pole-API's aanbieden. De engineeringuitdaging is de vertaling tussen endpointgerichte API-resources en het IFSF-database-/berichtmodel zonder directe vervanging van veldapparatuur af te dwingen.",
  "C++11 · legacy drivers · 32-bit Windows · binary protocol structures": "C++11 · legacy-drivers · 32-bit Windows · binaire protocolstructuren",
  "The system must preserve compatibility with established field hardware and legacy development constraints while handling acknowledgements, responses, binary data formats, simulator validation, and portability work.": "Het systeem moet compatibiliteit behouden met bestaande veldhardware en legacy-ontwikkelbeperkingen en tegelijk acknowledgements, responses, binaire dataformaten, simulatorvalidatie en overdraagbaarheidswerk afhandelen.",
  "Conversion path and protocol handling": "Conversiepad en protocolafhandeling",
  "Implemented work across the REST/Oat++ boundary, IFSF message construction and parsing, data conversion, acknowledgement flows, response handling, concurrency/message-pump behavior, and simulator-driven validation.": "Werk geïmplementeerd rond de REST-/Oat++-grens, opbouw en parsing van IFSF-berichten, dataconversie, acknowledgement-stromen, response-afhandeling, concurrency-/message-pumpgedrag en simulatorgestuurde validatie.",
  "Preserve OT behind a modern API boundary": "Behoud OT achter een moderne API-grens",
  "ILAC isolates conversion responsibility rather than requiring installed equipment to be replaced. The architecture preserves the existing C++11/legacy environment while exposing a modern REST-facing boundary.": "ILAC isoleert de verantwoordelijkheid voor conversie in plaats van vervanging van geïnstalleerde apparatuur te vereisen. De architectuur behoudt de bestaande C++11-/legacy-omgeving en biedt tegelijk een moderne REST-gerichte grens.",
  "OpenRetailing Price Pole APIs → REST/HTTP → ILAC → IFSF messages → LonTalk / TP/FT-10 → Price Pole": "OpenRetailing Price Pole-API's → REST/HTTP → ILAC → IFSF-berichten → LonTalk / TP/FT-10 → Price Pole",
  "Oat++ exposes the HTTP boundary; ILAC maps API resources to IFSF Database Address (DB_Ad) + Data Identifier (Data_Id) operations, sends the corresponding application messages over LonTalk / TP/FT-10, and converts responses back into API data.": "Oat++ biedt de HTTP-grens; ILAC koppelt API-resources aan IFSF Database Address (DB_Ad) + Data Identifier (Data_Id)-operaties, verstuurt de bijbehorende applicatieberichten via LonTalk / TP/FT-10 en converteert responses terug naar API-data.",
